            <ArticleTitle>A phytobezoar in the acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e21-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.amjsurg.2008.02.013</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A phytobezoar is a rare differential diagnosis in the acute abdomen. An 89-year-old woman presented with lower abdominal pain. A computed tomography scan and ultrasound suggested the presence of a bezoar. A phytobezoar was extracted surgically, and a resection was performed of the perforated small bowel segment. The etiology and management of phytobezoars are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
